I encountered NO problems getting beyond the "Loading sym53c8xx driver"
message, no matter what I did WRT termination on the SCSI bus. That is:

	active termination
	terminate on CDROM
	active AND terminate on CDROM
	no termination at all

They all "just worked" for me.

Note that I didn't fiddle with termination jumpers on the NCR875;
both TERMHIGH and TERMLOW were jumpered, and I connected all the
devices on one 68-pin cable with a 68->50 adapter at the CDROM,
