I'm suspecting that perhaps your DVD-ROM drive is the culprit, for
some reason, or perhaps some aspect of termination that I didn't think
of trying. It's certainly been the case in the past where the Linux
SCSI drivers were more sensitive to termination issues than the Tru64
or SRM ones, as well as being "changeable", ie some versions of a
driver would work with funky termination and other versions of the
same driver wouldn't.

