On Fri, 22 Oct 2004 11:30:57 +0200, Padiyath Sreekumaran
<kumar.padiyath at psi.ch> wrote:
>   Burned the fircd CD.
>   When I execute the command in SRM mode I get the following error:
> 
>   >boot dka400 -fi "kernels/vmlinux.gz" -fl "root=/dev/scd0"

Try not specifying the boot file and flags like that - aboot has all
those predefined in its config file. Try (assuming graphical install):
> boot dka400 -fi "" -fl "0"

The "0" is the number of the aboot config line to use. For a text mode
install, use:
> boot dka400 -fi "" -fl "0"



